## Installed, target and first-delivery boundaries

{{stable-verification-clock}}–{{plans-and-quality}} build the approved local pilot, with operator commands ({{operator-commands}}), live probes ({{live-feasibility-probes}}), the early real-data marketer check ({{early-marketer-checkpoint}}) and the browser checkpoint ({{interaction-checkpoint}}). They include configuration, a tested client foundation, automated interpretation, pilot-scale retrieval, real automation with lifecycle maintenance, email transport code, the interactive graph, conversation storage, live-window comparability and monitoring history, engagement and semantic-shift methods, progressive acquisition and operator controls. {{provider-readiness}}–{{email-readiness}} record per-capability provider/billing/send readiness, and {{human-pilot-acceptance}} is the live-data pilot release record. Software can be built before those records exist. A live capability or accepted pilot cannot be claimed before its relevant readiness evidence exists.

Core FR-C02/C03 and FR-P03/P04/P05/P06 stay in pilot build specifications. They are not moved to an optional proposal category because the code is currently narrow. Each method/route may remain visibly unavailable until its real source or evaluation prerequisite is met. The oEmbed and tiktok-web adapters exist for supplied references but are not task-integrated; {{source-capabilities}} describes them truthfully and {{supplementary-detail-route}} task-integrates one named detail route (default Bright Data profile/post detail fields). Supporting every conceivable provider is not a first-delivery requirement.

The bounded rule/LLM recommendation and extractive answer workflows satisfy useful core paths while keeping their actual limits, provided retrieval reaches the relevant support ({{pilot-scale-retrieval}}) and discovered posts carry interpretations ({{automated-interpretation}}). More fluent synthesis, semantic retrieval depth, richer creator factors and portfolio optimization remain explicit later paths under {{evaluated-retrieval}}–{{enable-richer-agent}}/{{objective-portfolios}}. Wider multimodal ontology, hosted tenancy, observed commerce and causal methods retain their own prerequisites in {{hosted-actors-tenancy}}–{{causal-measurement}}.

## Verification limits

The shared check runs pytest with `--maxfail=1`. The inherited run stopped at the first failure, `tests/test_assistant_enrichment.py:261`, where a fixed October 1 capture exceeds the freshness threshold, so the state of the rest of the suite is unknown until {{stable-verification-clock}}'s full inventory. [Development guidance](../docs/development.md#current-test-fixture-limitation) documents that one limitation. {{stable-verification-clock}} inventories the suite and fixes the clock-aging class without weakening freshness, retention or window policy.

[Planning verification](verification/verification-results.txt) checks this package's links, dependency order and rationale, decision references and complete traceability. Static repository checks are separately recorded in [static-check-results.txt](verification/static-check-results.txt). Neither proves the proposed architecture, provider readiness, production UI behavior or human usefulness. No browser, paid source/model call, email, commit or deployment is part of this planning work.
